       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This is about twice that limit.\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg in one dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 to 1,000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** A dose this high raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release)\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, if you want something different\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
